Third-party components
----------------------
Three node packs are kept under comfyui_nodes/third_party/ as a fallback for when their repository
is unreachable. They are the work of their own authors and stay under their own licences; each folder
keeps its LICENSE file, and they are not covered by the Apache-2.0 licence above.

  ComfyUI-Viggle-Animate-H3     Apache-2.0
  ComfyUI-sol-attn              Apache-2.0
  ComfyUI-NLF-Minimal           Apache-2.0 (derived from kijai/ComfyUI-WanVideoWrapper, MTV/nodes.py)

Every other pack is cloned from its own repository at a recorded commit when you run
tools/install_comfyui_nodes.py (see tools/comfyui_setup/setup.json) and is not part of this repository:

  ComfyUI-Frame-Interpolation   MIT
  ComfyUI-H3-AudioRefine        MIT
  ComfyUI-WanAnimatePreprocess  Apache-2.0
  comfyui_controlnet_aux        Apache-2.0
  comfyui-kjnodes               GPL-3.0
  comfyui-videohelpersuite      GPL-3.0 (one local patch: tools/comfyui_setup/patches/)
  ComfyUI-SCAIL-Pose            declares no licence (one local patch: tools/comfyui_setup/patches/)

The small patch files under tools/comfyui_setup/patches/ are kept here so the installer can apply them
to those clones.

Python dependencies keep their own licences (see backend/requirements.txt). Note that nudenet is
AGPL-3.0.

